<main class="lp-page belkins-salesroads-page" id="simple-guide">
  <div class="lp-hero-shell"><div class="lp-wrap">
    <nav class="lp-breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/">Home</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <a href="/resources/outbound-sales-library/">Outbound Sales Library</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <span aria-current="page">Belkins vs SalesRoads</span>
    </nav>
    <div class="lp-hero">
      <div>
        <h1>Belkins vs <span>SalesRoads</span>
          <small>Pricing and appointment setting</small>
        </h1>
        <p class="lp-intro">If you need people to call buyers and follow through, start with CallTeam’s managed calling quote. Compare it with Belkins’ quoted calling tier and SalesRoads’ dedicated rep.</p>
        <div class="lp-actions">
          <a class="lp-button" href="#comparison">Compare prices and scope</a>
          <a class="lp-text-link" href="#belkins-vs-salesroads-video" data-inline-play>Watch CallTeam’s process</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <aside class="lp-brief" aria-labelledby="buying-fit">
        <h2 id="buying-fit">What each price buys</h2>
        <dl class="bsr-verdict">
          <div><dt>CallTeam</dt><dd>From US{{ prices.callteamMonthly }} a month. Our callers make live calls, return callbacks and leave live voicemails or approved voicemail drops.</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Belkins</dt><dd>Belkins starts at {{ prices.belkinsMonthly }} a month. Get a separate Growth Plus quote if you want cold calling and voicemail. Belkins leaves that tier’s price open.</dd></div>
          <div><dt>SalesRoads</dt><dd>One dedicated rep costs {{ prices.salesroadsFourWeekRate }} every four weeks. Pay for that setup if you need an assigned SDR and email outreach.</dd></div>
        </dl>
      </aside>
    </div>
    <p class="lp-method">CallTeam publishes this guide and sells managed calling. Prices checked <time datetime="{{ guide.checkedDate }}">{{ guide.checkedLabel }}</time>. <a href="#sources">See the sources</a>.</p>
  </div></div>

  <nav class="lp-jump" aria-label="On this page"><div class="lp-wrap">
    <a href="#comparison">Price table</a><a href="#callteam">CallTeam video</a><a href="#budget">Budget examples</a><a href="#quote">Compare quotes</a><a href="#questions">FAQs</a>
  </div></nav>

  <section class="lp-section" id="comparison"><div class="lp-wrap">
    <div class="lp-heading"><h2>Belkins vs SalesRoads pricing and scope</h2></div>
    <div class="sg-table-wrap">
      <table class="lp-table sg-table" role="table">
        <caption>Published starting prices and included work</caption>
        <thead><tr role="row">
          <th scope="col" role="columnheader">Offer</th>
          <th scope="col" role="columnheader">Starting price</th>
          <th scope="col" role="columnheader">Outreach</th>
          <th scope="col" role="columnheader">Term and billing</th>
        </tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr role="row">
            <th scope="row" role="rowheader">Belkins managed</th>
            <td role="cell" data-label="Starting price"><strong>{{ prices.belkinsMonthly }} per month</strong></td>
            <td role="cell" data-label="Outreach">Email and LinkedIn. Growth lists calls tied to buyer signals. Growth Plus lists cold calling and voicemail.</td>
            <td role="cell" data-label="Term and billing">Belkins describes a six-month agreement with a month-three opt-out checkpoint.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr role="row">
            <th scope="row" role="rowheader">Belkins pay per appointment</th>
            <td role="cell" data-label="Starting price"><strong>{{ prices.belkinsAppointment }} per appointment</strong><br>{{ prices.belkinsSetup }} setup. Minimum {{ prices.packageMeetings }} appointments.</td>
            <td role="cell" data-label="Outreach">Email and LinkedIn with reply handling and booking.</td>
            <td role="cell" data-label="Term and billing">Package has a six-month delivery window from launch. Setup fee is non-refundable.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr role="row">
            <th scope="row" role="rowheader">SalesRoads dedicated SDR</th>
            <td role="cell" data-label="Starting price"><strong>{{ prices.salesroadsFourWeeks }} per four weeks</strong><br>One dedicated sales development rep.</td>
            <td role="cell" data-label="Outreach">Phone and email. LinkedIn is used for research.</td>
            <td role="cell" data-label="Term and billing">Four-week billing. SalesRoads advertises cancellation at any time.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr role="row">
            <th scope="row" role="rowheader">CallTeam managed calling</th>
            <td role="cell" data-label="Starting price"><strong>US{{ prices.callteamMonthly }} per month</strong></td>
            <td role="cell" data-label="Outreach">Human callers qualify buyers, schedule the next step and give sales the context in your CRM.</td>
            <td role="cell" data-label="Term and billing">Monthly program. Your written quote shows the included calling and follow-up, plus any fees for list research or extra coverage.</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="sg-sources"><a href="{{ sources.belkinsRetainer.url }}">Belkins managed rate and term</a> · <a href="{{ sources.belkinsPackage.url }}">Belkins appointment package</a> · <a href="{{ sources.salesroadsPricing.url }}">SalesRoads pricing</a> · <a href="/pricing/">CallTeam pricing</a></p>
  </div></section>

  <section class="lp-section lp-paper" id="callteam"><div class="lp-wrap">
    <div class="lp-heading">
      <h2>What CallTeam learns on a live call</h2>
      <p>A live caller can ask who owns the decision, what prompted the interest and when it makes sense to talk. We build a prospect list or work your accounts and agree with you on what qualifies a meeting.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="sg-two bsr-proof">
      {{ processVideoPreview("Watch CallTeam’s 78-second calling process", "See what happens from choosing the first accounts to briefing your salesperson.", "belkins-vs-salesroads") }}
      <article class="lp-pair-card">
        <h3>11 qualified SaaS demos in 90 days</h3>
        <p>Four buyers advanced to sales opportunities. Two became customers within six months.</p>
        <p>Our callers checked the buyer’s use case before booking. Sales received what the prospect wanted to see in the demo.</p>
        <a href="/case-studies/saas-demo-appointment-setting/">Read the SaaS campaign case study</a>
      </article>
    </div>
    <p class="bsr-follow-up">We log the reason for a callback and when the buyer asked us to try again. When a meeting is booked, sales gets the buyer’s reason to talk and any open questions. <a href="/services/b2b-cold-calling/">See our managed calling service</a>.</p>
    <div class="sg-mid-cta">
      <p><strong>Bring one target account.</strong> We’ll walk through who we’d call, what we’d ask and what the work would cost.</p>
      <a class="lp-button" href="https://calendly.com/hello-callteam/new-meeting" data-booking-placement="belkins-vs-salesroads">Book a free 30-minute call</a>
    </div>
  </div></section>

  <section class="lp-section" id="budget"><div class="lp-wrap">
    <div class="lp-heading">
      <h2>What to budget for three billing periods</h2>
      <p>These examples use published starting rates before taxes or quoted extras. Confirm Belkins’ and SalesRoads’ billing currency in writing.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="sg-table-wrap">
      <table class="lp-table sg-table" role="table">
        <caption>Example budgets by billing period</caption>
        <thead><tr role="row"><th scope="col" role="columnheader">Offer</th><th scope="col" role="columnheader">Billing period</th><th scope="col" role="columnheader">Example total</th><th scope="col" role="columnheader">What to check</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr role="row"><th scope="row" role="rowheader">Belkins managed</th><td role="cell" data-label="Billing period">Three calendar months</td><td role="cell" data-label="Example total"><strong>{{ prices.belkinsThree }}</strong></td><td role="cell" data-label="What to check">Six invoices at the floor total {{ prices.belkinsSix }}. Get checkpoint notice and exit terms in writing.</td></tr>
          <tr role="row"><th scope="row" role="rowheader">Belkins starter package</th><td role="cell" data-label="Billing period">{{ prices.packageMeetings }} appointments plus setup</td><td role="cell" data-label="Example total"><strong>{{ prices.packageTotal }}</strong></td><td role="cell" data-label="What to check">{{ prices.packageUnit }} per package slot with setup at the advertised floor. Choose it when email and LinkedIn fit your buyers.</td></tr>
          <tr role="row"><th scope="row" role="rowheader">SalesRoads, one SDR</th><td role="cell" data-label="Billing period">Three four-week periods</td><td role="cell" data-label="Example total"><strong>{{ prices.salesroadsThree }}</strong></td><td role="cell" data-label="What to check">Three invoices cover 12 weeks. An uninterrupted 52-week run would cost {{ prices.salesroadsAnnual }} across 13 invoices.</td></tr>
          <tr role="row"><th scope="row" role="rowheader">CallTeam outbound calling</th><td role="cell" data-label="Billing period">Three calendar months</td><td role="cell" data-label="Example total"><strong>US{{ prices.callteamThree }}</strong></td><td role="cell" data-label="What to check">Starting scope. Get fresh list research and any extra coverage priced in the quote.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="lp-note">For monthly budgeting, SalesRoads’ one-rep rate works out to about <strong>{{ prices.salesroadsMonthEquivalent }} per calendar month</strong> if you run for 52 weeks. The actual invoice remains on a four-week cycle.</p>
    <div class="sg-two bsr-scope">
      <article class="lp-pair-card">
        <h3>Belkins charges by plan or by package</h3>
        <p>Get calling frequency, who gets called and who owns callbacks in the managed quote. The prepaid package has its own terms.</p>
        <p>If the package falls short after six months, Belkins says it first works to make up the difference. Unused slots may qualify for a partial refund.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="lp-pair-card">
        <h3>SalesRoads charges for assigned reps</h3>
        <p>The rate includes a strategist, coaching, research, CRM integration, phone and email. Its pricing page lists 500 prospect records per rep per month.</p>
        <p>Two reps cost {{ prices.salesroadsTwoReps }} every four weeks. Buy that coverage if you can keep both reps working qualified accounts.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div></section>

  <section class="lp-section lp-paper" id="quote"><div class="lp-wrap">
    <div class="lp-heading"><h2>Get the same three answers from each agency</h2></div>
    <ol class="bsr-buying-checks">
      <li><strong>What can we spend before we can exit?</strong> Get setup, minimum term, recurring invoices and notice dates on one page.</li>
      <li><strong>Who works the account after the first touch?</strong> Ask who owns callbacks, voicemail, rescheduling and the CRM notes.</li>
      <li><strong>What does sales get before a meeting?</strong> Ask for a redacted handoff. Look for the buyer’s role, the problem they raised and what they agreed to discuss.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>Compare actual spend against held meetings your team accepts. Use the <a href="/b2b-meeting-quality-check/">meeting quality check</a> to agree on that standard.</p>
    <div class="lp-actions">
      <a class="lp-button" href="/lead-generation-proposal-comparison/">Compare agency quotes</a>
      <a class="lp-text-link" href="/articles/b2b-cold-call-voicemail-scripts-that-create-a-reason-to-call-back/">See CallTeam’s voicemail examples</a>
    </div>
  </div></section>

  <section class="lp-section" id="questions"><div class="lp-wrap lp-faq-wrap">
    <div class="lp-heading"><h2>Belkins vs SalesRoads FAQs</h2></div>
    <div class="lp-faqs">{% for faq in guide.faqs %}<details><summary>{{ faq.q }}</summary><p>{{ faq.a }}</p></details>{% endfor %}</div>
  </div></section>

  <section class="lp-section lp-paper" id="sources"><div class="lp-wrap">
    <div class="lp-heading"><h2>Pricing sources and related comparisons</h2></div>
    <ul>{% for key, source in sources %}<li><a href="{{ source.url }}">{{ source.label }}</a></li>{% endfor %}</ul>
    <p>Read <a href="/compare/callteam-vs-belkins/">CallTeam vs Belkins</a>, <a href="/compare/callteam-vs-salesroads/">CallTeam vs SalesRoads</a> or the <a href="/resources/b2b-lead-generation-pricing-report/">B2B lead generation pricing report</a>.</p>
  </div></section>
</main>
